X:1
T:Love Foolosophy
C:Jamiroquai
M:4/4
O:England, 2001
N:Two verses and the chorus. Melody from the lead-vocal channel of a MIDI arrangement (hamienet.com, track 352558304645637, channel 3), moved down a major sixth from B minor to D minor so the lowest note lands on C4 (C4 to D5). Chords from its bass, guitar and electric piano channels, which push every change an eighth early; they are written on the downbeat here. A second, independent arrangement (track 353075749569224, channel 2, labeled Vocals) has the same contour but is sloppier: it often has a flat seventh (C-sharp here) and a flat fifth (A-flat) where this one has the scale note, so this channel is followed. Humanized onsets snapped to the sixteenth grid; releases up to an eighth short of the next note are filled in. The singer's syncopations (notes landing a sixteenth or an eighth before the beat) are kept as ties.
